{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "carepoint-api-v1",
    "name": "CarePoint API",
    "description": "CarePoint backend API \u2014 local development collection.\n\nImport, set the collection variables (or use the defaults), then run requests in order. Session cookies (`cp_access`, `cp_refresh`) are stored automatically by Postman's cookie jar after a successful Login / Verify email / Google sign-in.\n\nAll mutating requests must carry the header `X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest` (CSRF defense) \u2014 it is pre-set on each request.\n\nEMAIL CODES: with the default `MAIL_PROVIDER=log`, OTP codes are printed to the Spring Boot console \u2014 look for `MAIL(log-provider)`. Paste the 6-digit code into the `{{otpCode}}` variable (or edit the request body). Codes are valid 2 minutes, allow 4 wrong tries, and only 4 sends are permitted before a cooldown.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080"
    },
    {
      "key": "patientEmail",
      "value": "patient.demo@carepoint.test"
    },
    {
      "key": "patientPassword",
      "value": "Correct-Horse-9"
    },
    {
      "key": "otpCode",
      "value": "paste-6-digit-code-here"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Ping",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ping"
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status is 200\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Health",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/actuator/health"
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status is 200\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});"
